+# HaveAPI client dependency and provenance
+
+The frontend imports `AsyncClient` from the normal `haveapi-client` dependency.
+Authenticated and public API calls use this package through the WebUI request
+policy described in [API contracts](API_CONTRACTS.md). There is no separate pilot
+application or transport switch. BFF session and OAuth exchanges retain their
+existing implementation.
+
+## Source and archive
+
+The committed archive is
+`vendor/haveapi-client-f94e65e35166a0bf8048a27c9d57c7d36957d65b.tgz`,
+from [HaveAPI commit f94e65e35166a0bf8048a27c9d57c7d36957d65b](https://github.com/vpsfreecz/haveapi/commit/f94e65e35166a0bf8048a27c9d57c7d36957d65b),
+subdirectory `clients/js`. Its package name/version is `haveapi-client@0.29.0`.
+This is a source snapshot, not a new npm release. The source commit must remain
+published and reachable before this WebUI branch is ready for integration.
+
+The archive is 55,702 bytes and has SHA-256
+`41c3c3f16577dd7c8849f11615e3111302513af65a1e5640c9b121f772fb9975`.
+Its npm integrity is
+`sha512-aMx3ofhbRmF0JjfzUdgV3k4Oh1G/4U37uvmKvDLtX9J/5A/yy8a1GALHK6v54wJY0fU9mW2pX9kkfqBlMZOmJw==`.
+[The provenance manifest](../../vendor/haveapi-client-provenance.json) records
+all 51 packed files, their hashes, the source revision and toolchain. Every file
+was compared with its committed `clients/js` counterpart. The tarball has no
+`gitHead`; provenance comes from that comparison and the recorded build.
+The MIT license and original copyright notice are included as `LICENSE.txt`.
+
+HaveAPI's repository root is not an npm package; the package lives in `clients/js`.
+A relative, committed npm archive gives ordinary `npm ci`, CI and Nix the same
+bytes without a local checkout, registry publication or expiring CI download.
+`package-lock.json` pins the archive integrity and its `xmlhttprequest@1.8.0`
+transitive dependency. The package's `latest` constraint does not float during
+`npm ci`.
+
+## Regenerating an intentional update
+
+Use a clean checkout of the selected published HaveAPI revision and its locked
+Nix shell. The recorded build used Node 24.21.0, npm 11.19.0 and TypeScript 5.9.3;
+the tracked client lockfile had SHA-256
+`1c7f66cccadc6abf9474d3403db38ce524aa49d3352efb19596aa86ffeaaaec6`.
+From the HaveAPI repository root, create an empty output directory outside the
+checkout, export `OUT` with its absolute path, then run:
+
+```sh
+export OUT=/absolute/path/to/output
+nix develop .#client-js -c bash
+cd clients/js
+npm ci
+npm run build
+git diff --exit-code
+npm pack --json --pack-destination "$OUT"
+```
+
+Inspect the npm pack manifest, reconcile every packed file with the selected
+commit, and record source, tools, license, file hashes and archive integrity.
+Copy the resulting archive without changing its bytes to a filename containing
+the full source commit. Update the relative dependency using the pinned WebUI npm
+toolchain, preserving unrelated lock entries. The archive in this repository is
+the authoritative byte artifact; a later repack must be checked rather than
+assumed byte-identical.
+
+## Installation, Nix and verification
+
+Ordinary development and CI use `nix develop` and `npm ci --include=dev`.
+There is no extra package installer. The [package guide](PACKAGING.md) explains
+Nix's standard `importNpmLock` hook and the exact committed archive override.
+The frontend's source check verifies dependency/provenance agreement and archive
+SHA-256/npm integrity before installation. It rejects missing or altered bytes.
+The original root manifest and lockfile remain unchanged by the Nix build.
+
+Typechecking and API tests use the actual installed declarations and client.
+Controlled XHR fixtures exercise production request paths, session renewal,
+public calls, abort and rejection semantics. Ordinary application browser
+workflows provide browser coverage; there is no standalone candidate entry.
+After committed-deliverable review, run the normal full tests, production build
+and Nix frontend/source/package checks. Fixtures establish their stated scope;
+they do not certify live OAuth, backend permissions or a deployed application.
+
+The [dated pilot record](../work-log/2026-10-19-haveapi-package-pilot.md) preserves
+prior package-fit evidence and its original source/archive identities. That
+pilot is superseded by this production dependency; its historical checks are not
+fresh verification of this revision. Dependency changes do not deploy the WebUI.
