+# Production HaveAPI client replacement: 2026-10-20
+
+## Request and implementation
+
+REQ-007, REQ-011, REQ-012 and REQ-059; PR74. The maintainer requested a complete
+replacement of the original WebUI client rather than a trial. Normal authenticated,
+public and description requests now use the actual installed HaveAPI AsyncClient.
+The custom fetch transport, duplicate encoder/decoder and injection factory are
+removed. The dependency/provenance change and obsolete pilot removal accompany
+this source change; the [provenance guide](../design/HAVEAPI_CLIENT.md)
+records their owning build inputs.
+
+WebUI keeps domain-helper signatures, metadata/single-namespace projection,
+live auth headers, per-call language, BFF renewal, mutation non-replay, uncertain
+outcomes, abort and action-state receipts. Description fallback uses a library
+OPTIONS request at the versioned base. Public clients remain anonymous and do not
+discover descriptions or recover sessions. No library setup/authenticate call or
+cached token is used. BFF JSON/OAuth requests remain separate protocols.
+
+Domain fixtures now exercise real package serialization and validation through a
+stable controlled XHR. Core cases cover original getter/query/language snapshots,
+fresh auth on one read retry, public separation, relative bases, OPTIONS discovery,
+nested rejection, malformed 401 responses without recovery, unusable success payloads,
+receipts, native network failure and abort. Ordinary app fixtures serve enveloped
+OPTIONS descriptions; home/public smoke assertions check native XHR and auth
+separation without a pilot entry or test-only application interface.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+The focused actual-package run passed all 39 changed API test files (289 cases)
+in 9.52 seconds against the installed final dependency. Application and tooling
+TypeScript checks passed, as did the E2E core check with public overview adopted
+into its strict coverage (61 checked, 202 deferred). Design inventory and the
+118-document audit, Tailwind/pattern checks, scoped lint/format and structural
+budgets passed. The initial domain run exposed fetch-specific assertions; these
+now check decoded query values, JSON MIME type with charset and actual XHR abort,
+without changing request values or cancellation policy. Its failed logs are
+retained in local session evidence.
+
+Independent final review, full application tests/build, Nix frontend/package
+verification and ordinary browser workflows remain pending. Historical pilot
+results do not certify this production replacement.
+
+The source change requires no backend schema or stored-session migration. Existing
+services retain their wire contract; a rollback restores the matching prior
+frontend package and lock. Synthetic fixtures do not certify OAuth exchange,
+backend permissions or live task completion. PR74 remains open; no merge, release
+or deployment is claimed.
